Z||000009||DaRkLoRD||12-26-2000||05:14 PM||||The reason electric cars have so far been this inefficient, is because most people are unwilling to give up the instant power of a gasoline engine, to actually work with and develop a better electric vehicle. You think gasoline engines are gonna be around forever?<P>I doubt they'll last another 20 years.. and personally, I can't wait.... as long as gasoline engines aren't made illegal in the process of phasing them out. I would love to see average people driving electric cars, and auto enthusaists have gasoline cars for recreational use, the same way horse owners do today..<P>it'll be a long time before an electric vehicle can outrun a gasoline vehicle... but think about this, electric cars are fairly new.. 20 years ago they were practically unheard of. Gasoline engines, on the other hand, have had over 100 years of development....<P>Just for the record, I plan on converting a small economy car to run on hydrogen, supplemented by alcohol. an average sized car only needs about 15hp to maintain highway cruising speed. It's accelerating that takes all the power. By using alcohol to fuel acceleration, and switching over to hydrogen for cruising, the mileage would be incredible... with practically no harmful emissions. (this would be a project... not as a daily driver!!!!!)<P>so, while I probably wouldn't convert a Fiero to electric.... I wouldn't laugh at a guy for doing so. If we all cared enough about the environment to do something like this, we might actually slow down the destruction of our planet.. I don't know about other young people here, but I eventually want to have kids. If the pollution continues at the same rate it is today (which is better than it used to be a few years ago, but still too much..) I'm scared to think of what the air quality will be in 10, 20 or 30 years....<P>sorry for the rant.. <P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 12-26-2000).]||||reg||8
