Z||000013||rockcrawl||12-26-2000||08:59 PM||||There are several drawbacks to electric cars as I see it. First of all, the majority of american drivers demand a vehicle with performance that an electric cannot supply. Second, It takes energy to charge all those batteries. An electric car does not pollute directly, but the power station that supplies the electricity does. If we woke up tomorrow and every car was electric, there would be a complete blackout across the nation. Of course there is hydroelectric and solar power, but not enough to power the world.<P>Another interesting note: Recently I was at a Toyota training center in NJ. I got to take a look at the new Toyota Prius. It has an electric drive motor and an enviro friendly NIMH battery. It also has a small gas engine attached to the transaxle, not to drive the wheels, but to power a generator. It's funny seeing a transaxle with heavy electrical cables coming out of it. The battery is charged entirely by the onboard generator, no need to plug it in at night. I think it gets something like 70-90 MPG. I didn't get a chance to drive it, but they said its pretty snappy. It was also equipped with toyotas navigational system with GPS and color touch-screen monitor which doubles as the stereo. <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000014||StuGood||12-26-2000||10:35 PM||||I have to admire these pioneer types who go off and design prototype electric vehicles and such.  I agree with RC; we don't probably have the infrastructure (today) to support an all-electric vehicle fleet.  But remember, there was a time (not terribly long ago), we didn't produce a <B>drop</B> of gasoline, and nobody ever heard of service stations.<P>FWIW, some of the hybrid vehicles concepts are of the most interest to me.  One thing is certain: the guy that goes off and actually designs and <B>builds</B> a working prototype, gains more practical knowledge than I can shake a slipstick at  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ||||reg||6
